# Original real smooth product coordinates for the elliptic fillings

The actual varying period family is real smoothly marked by any fixed
original period torus.  The exact previously constructed full and small
elliptic-cap products are real smooth diffeomorphisms for the original
complex atlases with scalars restricted to the real field.  Their inverses,
original quotient representatives, and native boundary product are retained.

These are construction-specific smooth local models.  No cusp extension,
completed global Seifert quotient, or recognition of the threefold as the
standard smooth sphere is asserted here.
-/
